diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index c948b06..435af8d 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -2,4 +2,22 @@
 
 Runs lint, tests, and a scheduled CodeQL analysis.
 
-Actions are referenced by major version tag. There is no Dependabot configuration.
+## How action updates are handled
+
+Every action in `.github/workflows/` is pinned to a full 40-character commit SHA,
+with the release version in a trailing comment (for example
+`actions/checkout@<sha> # v7.0.1`). Tags are mutable, so a SHA is the only
+reference that cannot be moved after review.
+
+[Dependabot](.github/dependabot.yml) keeps those pins current:
+
+- It checks the `github-actions` ecosystem weekly.
+- All updates are grouped into a single pull request.
+- A 7-day cooldown means a release is only proposed once it has been public for a
+  week, which leaves time for a malicious release to be found and withdrawn.
+- Dependabot rewrites both the SHA and the version comment.
+
+When reviewing the weekly pull request, read the upstream diff between the old and
+new SHAs and the release notes for any major-version bump, rather than trusting the
+version number. Merge it promptly; a pinned action does not otherwise update itself.
+When adding a new action, pin it to a SHA resolved from its repository, not a tag.
